       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4000 mg four times daily is 16,000 mg/day, which is five times the maximum daily ibuprofen dose. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for outpatients and 2,400 mg/day in most inpatient protocols. A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day), a common dose\n- **800 mg** PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg** PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 4000 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest pharmacy review before it's entered."
